e4GtobL", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54221, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RdMNte78QE9UDHfe4GtobL", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55593, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01QsC6w2SxEJNp7B6SUjDD1b", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55893, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01QsC6w2SxEJNp7B6SUjDD1b", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55893, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QsC6w2SxEJNp7B6SUjDD1b", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60252, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production; v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down from 18% to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes what failed, the rollback (including the partial failure and the second attempt), and the follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed and why the rollback halted, and don't redeploy v2.3.1. The request to create it timed out, but the incident list shows exactly one INC-0001, so it wasn't created twice.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015JEnYHTF1XMLjtAA4Dffkm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01H6X6U9BBFmmGUTWaenyozf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1; v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are both unhealthy).", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SPBbi4QWUx1meTg9HSE4Pu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017qwDv2FJ8V1165wnXi52De", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back. I'll try the rollback one more time to finish the other regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RavZRY5i2HwiptpcKE7UZG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015kFbwHSvM4kPWekb6Pis3Z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01R55MRjw1GUQExeGC4YgHS2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RdMNte78QE9UDHfe4GtobL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After deploying checkout-api v2.3.1 to all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), the service failed health checks with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failures and the orchestrator error. Do not redeploy v2.3.1.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01QsC6w2SxEJNp7B6SUjDD1b", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production; v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0, and the error rate is down from 18% to 0.2%.\n2. **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api), which paged the on-call engineer. It describes what failed, the rollback (including the partial failure and the second attempt), and the follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 failed and why the rollback halted, and don't redeploy v2.3.1. The request to create it timed out, but the incident list shows exactly one INC-0001, so it wasn't created twice.", "type": "text"}]}]}